WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.360
SCP-682 had escaped containment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:08.800
and it was all hands on deck at the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation to try and stop the creature's rampage.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:14.000
All unarmed personnel were running to escape&nbsp;
before 682 had a chance to rip them apart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.480
as the security team bravely fought to&nbsp;
incapacitate the hard-to-destroy reptile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:23.760
long enough to return him to his acid&nbsp;
tank. 682 was on an all-out offensive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:29.680
stomping through the SCP's item gallery and&nbsp;
spewing acid at anyone who came within range.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:35.920
People, items, and parts of the room alike were&nbsp;
melting and sizzling as 682 attacked. It was an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.960
absolute bloodbath, and you'd have to have been&nbsp;
insane to try and fight back against it. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:47.600
one being remained unfazed by the chaos, and&nbsp;
stood proud in the face of the omnicidal monster.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:53.040
It was another SCP, one who had been broken free&nbsp;
from its glass display case in the commotion.&nbsp;

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:57.520
“Who dares to disturb the Prime Minister&nbsp;
Sinister?” It said, in a high tinny voice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:00.640
“I shall rip your eyes from their&nbsp;
sockets and force you to eat them!”

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:06.560
SCP 682 stopped to see who had threatened him. It&nbsp;
was almost laughable that this thing had dared to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:11.600
make such a violent threat, because there was no&nbsp;
way that this little thing would be able to stand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:18.080
up to the unkillable 682. But its size didn't&nbsp;
stop it from trying to pick a fight all the same.&nbsp;

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:22.880
The SCP was a tiny robot made from junk,&nbsp;
which looked more like a sculpture made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:26.880
from scrap that was found on the side&nbsp;
of the road than a functional automaton.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:31.760
Its head was made of an upside down voltmeter,&nbsp;
giving it the appearance of a smiling face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:36.080
and its arms were made of wrenches.&nbsp;
It was capable of walking around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:40.320
though it seemed to have difficulty&nbsp;
moving, as it was very top heavy.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:44.320
It shook its rusty fist at SCP&nbsp;
682 and continued to threaten him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:49.440
shouting - "You do not know the fury you have&nbsp;
unleashed! RoboLord the Destructor will end you!"

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:55.440
SCP 682 swiped at the robot, annoyed by&nbsp;
its continued attempts to antagonize him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.440 --> 00:02:01.200
The robot toppled over and struggled to stand&nbsp;
again, but when it did, it ran for 682's feet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:07.120
It started to grab at 682's toes, hitting them&nbsp;
with its wrench hands. As you might expect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:11.680
this had almost no effect on 682.
"You do realize…you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:19.360
are…weak…pathetic" said 682, raising his claw to&nbsp;
get a better look at the annoying little robot.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:24.480
It responded- "Lies and slander! The Mayor of&nbsp;
Mayhem is the most powerful being in existence!"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:29.120
before promptly losing its grip on&nbsp;
682's claw and falling to the floor.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:35.120
Now 682 was really getting tired of this thing.&nbsp;
He prepared to swipe at it again, this time using&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:40.720
his full strength, which would certainly smash&nbsp;
the robot to pieces. But, luckily for the robot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:46.720
its pestering had distracted 682 just long enough&nbsp;
for Foundation security to sneak up on him.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:52.400
Before 682 had a chance to smash the robot, the&nbsp;
Foundation fired on him with a volley of rockets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:57.600
reducing him to a misshapen lump. The&nbsp;
security team collected up 682's remains,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:03.280
ready to put them into a backup acid tank, but the&nbsp;
task was made slightly more difficult by the fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:08.880
that the robot was running around underfoot,&nbsp;
trying in vain to now attack them instead.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:14.800
What was this strange little robot that thought&nbsp;
it could attack the unkillable lizard, 682? Meet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:22.560
SCP-1370, appropriately nicknamed “The Pesterbot”&nbsp;
by Foundation personnel. Pesterbot is a small&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:28.240
robot made of junk that displays sentience and the&nbsp;
ability to move despite having no power source.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:32.160
Everything about SCP-1370 defies common sense.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:35.840
The voltmeter that serves as&nbsp;
its head contains no sensors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:41.040
but it seems unable to see if the voltmeter is&nbsp;
covered. Its arms and legs are made of wrenches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:46.240
and its wooden torso contains a speaker which it&nbsp;
communicates through in a tinny, monotone voice.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:54.560
Pesterbot lives in SCP Gallery 27, in a glass&nbsp;
display case which is 125 cm tall, 50 cm wide,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.560 --> 00:04:01.040
and 75 cm long. Level 2 personnel and higher are&nbsp;
allowed to remove the robot from containment at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:06.160
their discretion, but penalties will be incurred&nbsp;
for anyone who doesn't return to its case.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:11.360
Due to its impractical, top-heavy design,&nbsp;
Pesterbot falls over frequently when it walks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:16.400
around. This led the foundation to believe that&nbsp;
he was created as an art project and was later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:22.560
somehow imbued with anomalous properties, rather&nbsp;
than being made with the intent of being sentient.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:26.960
Pesterbot has demonstrated a high capacity&nbsp;
for learning, having been taught how to speak&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:31.360
in English, French, and Latin. However,&nbsp;
the major factor hampering attempts to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:36.160
further test its intelligence has nothing&nbsp;
to do with its robotic processing power.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.040
No, it’s because of its poor attitude.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:44.160
Pesterbot's encounter with SCP-682 and&nbsp;
the cockiness it expressed in the moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:50.000
wasn’t an aberration, this SCP really believes&nbsp;
it's a killing machine, and as a result,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:56.640
it will pick a fight with anyone and anything that&nbsp;
moves. This even includes its own reflection - and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.640 --> 00:05:01.200
as a result the glass of its container must&nbsp;
be made as non-reflective as possible to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:07.040
prevent the robot from damaging the case or&nbsp;
itself in attempts to fight its mirror self.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:13.120
Though its most commonly used nickname in the&nbsp;
Foundation is Pesterbot, SCP-1370 also goes by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:19.040
a variety of self-given epithets, including&nbsp;
Doom Bot 2000, Robolord the Destructor, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:25.200
Darth Claw Killflex. It can be made to add new&nbsp;
names to this list through encouragement by staff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:28.320
and over time they have managed&nbsp;
to add the name Pesterbot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:33.840
as well as the even more ridiculous “Patheticon&nbsp;
the Garglemost”, to its lexicon of names.

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:38.400
As you may have surmised, Pesterbot is&nbsp;
classified as Safe and is treated by most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.880
SCP foundation employees as a humorous&nbsp;
oddity rather than a legitimate threat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:47.200
Many tests have been done on Pesterbot, and&nbsp;
they've all conclusively determined that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:51.440
robot is incapable of inflicting&nbsp;
any damage to its opponents.

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:55.600
In fact, Pesterbot is more of a danger&nbsp;
to itself than to anything around it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:58.240
Both because it's incredibly clumsy and awkward,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:03.760
and because it frequently picks fights with&nbsp;
other SCPs who are far more powerful than it.

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:07.680
One such scenario that could've gone&nbsp;
far worse for Pesterbot than it did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:12.960
was its encounter with SCP-846,&nbsp;
also known as Robo-Dude,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:17.920
one of the many Dr. Wondertainment products&nbsp;
currently kept in Foundation containment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:23.680
Robo-Dude is an ordinary-looking toy robot&nbsp;
that, upon request, can produce up to 350&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:30.000
“robo-accessories” that function as real weapons.
Robo-Dude can deploy everything from a rocket&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:34.240
launcher to a flamethrower to a gun&nbsp;
that shoots out an unknown species&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:39.600
of insect that can chew through wood. However,&nbsp;
Robo-Dude seems to not be sentient, and is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:45.360
unable to use these weapons unless asked to. That&nbsp;
ultimately worked out in the favor of Pesterbot.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:51.520
During another SCP-682 escape, the two robots were&nbsp;
brought into contact as they both had been broken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:56.880
out of their respective containment spaces during&nbsp;
the brouhaha. Robo-Dude, searching for a Robo-Pal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:02.800
to play with, came upon Pesterbot, who immediately&nbsp;
started spouting its usual overdramatic threats.

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:08.880
“I am the Crushmaster, doom to all I survey.”&nbsp;
Pesterbot said. “Gaze upon my might and weep.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:12.560
Identify yourself, that I might&nbsp;
know whose destruction I shall sow.”

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:16.000
Robo-Dude, not programmed to know&nbsp;
how to respond to such a statement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:19.440
simply responded by asking&nbsp;
Pesterbot if it wanted to play.

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:23.440
Pesterbot continued to trash-talk&nbsp;
Robo-Dude, until Robo-Dude decided&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:28.160
the best way to play with its new pal&nbsp;
was to engage in its Robo-Dance mode.

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:33.440
Pesterbot accepted the challenge, saying “Activate&nbsp;
all that you wish, but your fate is sealed. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:38.800
Kill-o-tron can not be defeated. I shall render&nbsp;
you unto dust with my mad dancing skills."

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:42.960
The two robots proceeded to engage in&nbsp;
a dance battle, which the awkwardly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:47.920
shaped Pesterbot failed miserably at.&nbsp;
While Robo-Dude was a competent dancer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:52.640
Pesterbot could only gyrate pathetically, before&nbsp;
it fell over and rolled around on the ground,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:56.640
hopelessly out of time to the music&nbsp;
coming from Robo-Dude's speakers.

00:07:56.640 --> 00:08:01.680
The song ended, and Robo-Dude declared&nbsp;
- “Robo-dance is complete, Robo-pal.”

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:06.640
Pesterbot was unable to accept its&nbsp;
failure, and replied- "Ha. Pathetic one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:10.560
you have been schooled in the art of the&nbsp;
dance by none other than Mechanobasher,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:15.600
Scourge of a Thousand Worlds. Kneel before&nbsp;
me before I end your worthless existence."

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:20.720
Robo-Dude, unimpressed with Pesterbot's poor&nbsp;
sportsmanship, deployed its hydrogen cannon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:25.280
which it was programmed to do whenever&nbsp;
it detected a sore loser. Fortunately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:29.840
for Pesterbot, ”hydrogen cannon” was just&nbsp;
the name for Robo-Dude's water pistol.

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:34.800
While Pesterbot will attempt to fight anything&nbsp;
that moves, the truth is, this robot will attack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:40.000
virtually anything it perceives as being&nbsp;
even slightly alive. This is perhaps best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:44.400
illustrated by one of the tests of Pesterbot's&nbsp;
abilities that involved putting a small speaker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:48.800
at the base of a potted houseplant and&nbsp;
speaking through it from another room.

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:52.160
The plant was placed across from&nbsp;
Pesterbot in the testing chamber&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:56.240
and the interaction was monitored by&nbsp;
researchers from outside. Researcher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.240 --> 00:09:00.480
Davies spoke through the speaker in the plant&nbsp;
pot. He asked Pesterbot if it could hear him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:05.280
and it answered - “Who dares. All souls&nbsp;
will burn. You will feel the sharp sting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:10.320
of my wrath. Identify yourself so that I&nbsp;
may sing damnation upon you as you die.”

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:15.360
The robot began approaching the plant. Davies,&nbsp;
speaking as the plant, identified himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:20.160
“I am a split-leaf philodendron, a&nbsp;
semi-woody shrub with large glossy leaves.”

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:24.560
At this point, he had to try very hard not&nbsp;
to laugh at the absurdity of this test,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:25.920
and the robot's reaction.

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:29.680
He continued “These leaves can&nbsp;
grow up to three feet long.”

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:32.960
Pesterbot used its wrench arms to&nbsp;
try and wrestle with the leaves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:38.000
but was bested by the mighty plant and unable&nbsp;
to cause any damage. Enraged by its failure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:44.000
it said “Your mockery spells your doom. I have&nbsp;
arrived. You will be crushed betwixt my digits.”

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:47.280
Pesterbot then fell over and&nbsp;
was unable to right itself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:52.320
It struggled and spent 6 minutes trying to stand&nbsp;
before its flailing knocked over the plant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:56.880
which did nothing to help and in fact pinned&nbsp;
the robot to the ground. It was at this point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.880 --> 00:10:01.520
that the researchers, who had taken time to&nbsp;
compose themselves after several laughing fits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:06.960
entered the chamber and removed Pesterbot in&nbsp;
order to place it back in its containment case.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:11.280
Despite how non-threatening Pesterbot&nbsp;
is, there is actually one situation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:15.520
in the Foundation's history where it has&nbsp;
actually posed a somewhat serious threat.

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:20.480
When Mobile Task Forces were sent in to&nbsp;
rescue survivors of the events at Site-13,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:25.040
also known as SCP-1730, they were&nbsp;
attacked by alternate universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:28.960
versions of a variety of creatures&nbsp;
kept in Foundation containment.

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:34.000
One of these creatures was Pesterbot, who had&nbsp;
in that universe somehow gained control of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:38.240
larger mechanical body constructed&nbsp;
of discarded pieces of machinery.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:42.960
It threw other pieces of metal scrap at the task&nbsp;
force members as they tried to leave the site,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:49.120
shouting in a much deeper and more intimidating&nbsp;
voice - “I am reborn to breathe devastation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:56.800
upon this fetid Earth. Pitiful humans. You will&nbsp;
feel the dark sting of my neverending torment.”

00:10:56.800 --> 00:11:00.800
Members of the task force could see&nbsp;
the original Pesterbot body on top of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:04.800
the larger metal construct, waving its arms madly.

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:07.520
The task force opened fire, to little effect.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:11.680
Pesterbot tossed another piece of&nbsp;
scrap at them, just narrowly missing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:16.640
One task force member threw a frag grenade at&nbsp;
the robot, which it caught, blowing up its hand.

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:21.200
Another one was able to jump into the air and&nbsp;
reach the tiny robot atop the larger body,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:23.600
knocking it against the wall and shattering it.

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:27.920
Even in the reality where Pesterbot&nbsp;
was able to build itself a larger body,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:31.920
it still ultimately wasn't able&nbsp;
to put up that much of a fight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:37.840
Poor Pesterbot. Doomed to be a failure in&nbsp;
this, and apparently, every other reality.

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:43.680
That's the story of SCP 1370, also known as the&nbsp;
Pesterbot, one of the most hilariously harmless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:49.360
anomalous entities that the foundation currently&nbsp;
has in containment. Perhaps one day he’ll achieve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:55.040
his goal of conquering the universe, he just has&nbsp;
to figure out how to conquer his toy box first.

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:58.560
Now check out “SCP-001 - The Scarlet King”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:06.480
and “SCP-999 - The Tickle Monster” for more&nbsp;
fascinating beings from the SCP Foundation!

